{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Exploratory Analysis: UNSW-NB15 Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook provides an exploratory analysis of the UNSW-NB15 dataset\n",
    "for the Privacy-Preserving Network Anomaly Detection project.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Note:** All final experiments must be run via the Python pipeline (`python -m src.pipeline`)\n",
    "to ensure reproducibility. This notebook is for exploration and understanding only."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Setup\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, str(Path('..').resolve() / 'src'))\n",
    "\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import yaml\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set style\n",
    "plt.style.use('seaborn-v0_8-whitegrid')\n",
    "sns.set_palette('husl')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load config\n",
    "with open('../configs/config.yaml', 'r') as f:\n",
    "    config = yaml.safe_load(f)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Config loaded successfully')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Dataset Overview"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load raw data\n",
    "raw_dir = Path(config['dataset']['raw_dir'])\n",
    "train_file = config['dataset']['train_file']\n",
    "test_file = config['dataset']['test_file']\n",
    "\n",
    "train_path = raw_dir / train_file\n",
    "test_path = raw_dir / test_file\n",
    "\n",
    "if train_path.exists() and test_path.exists():\n",
    "    train_df = pd.read_csv(train_path, low_memory=False)\n",
    "    test_df = pd.read_csv(test_path, low_memory=False)\n",
    "    print(f'Training set: {train_df.shape[0]:,} rows × {train_df.shape[1]} columns')\n",
    "    print(f'Test set: {test_df.shape[0]:,} rows × {test_df.shape[1]} columns')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('Dataset files not found. Please download UNSW-NB15 dataset first.')\n",
    "    print(f'Expected at: {train_path} and {test_path}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Class Distribution"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if 'train_df' in locals():\n",
    "    target_col = config['target']['column']\n",
    "    \n",
    "    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for ax, df, title in [(axes[0], train_df, 'Training Set'), (axes[1], test_df, 'Test Set')]:\n",
    "        counts = df[target_col].value_counts().sort_index()\n",
    "        labels = ['Normal (0)', 'Anomaly (1)']\n",
    "        colors = ['#2ecc71', '#e74c3c']\n",
    "        \n",
    "        bars = ax.bar(labels, counts.values, color=colors, alpha=0.8)\n",
    "        ax.set_title(f'{title} - Class Distribution')\n",
    "        ax.set_ylabel('Count')\n",
    "        \n",
    "        for bar, count in zip(bars, counts.values):\n",
    "            ax.text(bar.get_x() + bar.get_width()/2, bar.get_height() + 50,\n",
    "                   f'{count:,} ({count/len(df):.1%})', ha='center', va='bottom')\n",
    "    \n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print('Training class distribution:')\n",
    "    print(train_df[target_col].value_counts())\n",
    "    print()\n",
    "    print('Test class distribution:')\n",
    "    print(test_df[target_col].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Feature Overview"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if 'train_df' in locals():\n",
    "    print('All columns:')\n",
    "    for i, col in enumerate(train_df.columns):\n",
    "        dtype = train_df[col].dtype\n",
    "        n_unique = train_df[col].nunique()\n",
    "        n_missing = train_df[col].isnull().sum()\n",
    "        print(f'  {i+1:2d}. {col:30s} | {str(dtype):10s} | unique: {n_unique:6d} | missing: {n_missing}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Missing Value Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if 'train_df' in locals():\n",
    "    missing = train_df.isnull().sum()\n",
    "    missing = missing[missing > 0].sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if len(missing) > 0:\n",
    "        print('Columns with missing values:')\n",
    "        for col, count in missing.items():\n",
    "            pct = count / len(train_df) * 100\n",
    "            print(f'  {col:30s}: {count:6d} ({pct:.2f}%)')\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print('No missing values in training set')\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Also check test set\n",
    "    missing_test = test_df.isnull().sum()\n",
    "    missing_test = missing_test[missing_test > 0].sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "    if len(missing_test) > 0:\n",
    "        print('\\nTest set missing values:')\n",
    "        for col, count in missing_test.items():\n",
    "            pct = count / len(test_df) * 100\n",
    "            print(f'  {col:30s}: {count:6d} ({pct:.2f}%)')\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print('\\nNo missing values in test set')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Feature Distributions (Selected Metadata Features)"
   ]
  ],
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if 'train_df' in locals():\n",
    "    # Select key metadata features for visualization\n",
    "    metadata_features = [\n",
    "        'dur', 'spkts', 'dpkts', 'sbytes', 'dbytes', 'rate',\n",
    "        'sttl', 'dttl', 'sload', 'dload',\n",
    "        'sinpkt', 'dinpkt', 'sjit', 'djit',\n",
    "        'tcprtt', 'synack', 'ackdat',\n",
    "        'proto', 'service', 'state'\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    available = [f for f in metadata_features if f in train_df.columns]\n",
    "    print(f'Available metadata features: {len(available)}/{len(metadata_features)}')\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Plot numeric features\n",
    "    numeric_features = [f for f in available if train_df[f].dtype in ['int64', 'float64', 'int32', 'float32']]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    n_features = len(numeric_features)\n",
    "    n_cols = 4\n",
    "    n_rows = (n_features + n_cols - 1) // n_cols\n",
    "    \n",
    "    fig, axes = plt.subplots(n_rows, n_cols, figsize=(16, 4*n_rows))\n",
    "    axes = axes.flatten() if n_rows > 1 else [axes] if n_cols == 1 else axes\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for i, feat in enumerate(numeric_features):\n",
    "        ax = axes[i]\n",
    "        # Plot by class\n",
    "        for cls, color, label in [(0, '#2ecc71', 'Normal'), (1, '#e74c3c', 'Anomaly')]:\n",
    "            data = train_df[train_df['label'] == cls][feat]\n",
    "            ax.hist(data, bins=50, alpha=0.5, label=label, color=color, density=True)\n",
    "        ax.set_title(feat)\n",
    "        ax.set_xlabel('Value')\n",
    "        ax.set_ylabel('Density')\n",
    "        ax.legend(fontsize=8)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Hide unused subplots\n",
    "    for i in range(n_features, len(axes)):\n",
    "        axes[i].set_visible(False)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Categorical Feature Distributions"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if 'train_df' in locals():\n",
    "    categorical_features = ['proto', 'service', 'state']\n",
    "    available_cat = [f for f in categorical_features if f in train_df.columns]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, len(available_cat), figsize=(5*len(available_cat), 5))\n",
    "    if len(available_cat) == 1:\n",
    "        axes = [axes]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for i, feat in enumerate(available_cat):\n",
    "        ax = axes[i]\n",
    "        # Stacked bar chart by class\n",
    "        ct = pd.crosstab(train_df[feat], train_df['label'], normalize='index')\n",
    "        ct.plot(kind='bar', stacked=True, ax=ax, color=['#2ecc71', '#e74c3c'])\n",
    "        ax.set_title(f'{feat} - Class Distribution')\n",
    "        ax.set_xlabel(feat)\n",
    "        ax.set_ylabel('Proportion')\n",
    "        ax.legend(['Normal', 'Anomaly'])\n",
    "        ax.tick_params(axis='x', rotation=45)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Feature Correlation (Numeric Features)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if 'train_df' in locals():\n",
    "    # Select numeric metadata features\n",
    "    full_metadata = config['feature_sets']['FULL_METADATA']\n",
    "    numeric_metadata = [f for f in full_metadata if f in train_df.columns and train_df[f].dtype in ['int64', 'float64', 'int32', 'float32']]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Sample for faster computation\n",
    "    sample_df = train_df[numeric_metadata].sample(n=min(5000, len(train_df)), random_state=42)\n",
    "    corr = sample_df.corr()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Plot heatmap\n",
    "    plt.figure(figsize=(14, 12))\n",
    "    mask = np.triu(np.ones_like(corr, dtype=bool))\n",
    "    sns.heatmap(corr, mask=mask, cmap='RdBu_r', center=0,\n",
    "                square=True, linewidths=0.5, cbar_kws={'shrink': 0.8},\n",
    "                xticklabels=True, yticklabels=True)\n",
    "    plt.title('Feature Correlation Matrix (Numeric Metadata Features)')\n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # High correlations\n",
    "    print('High correlations (|r| > 0.8):')\n",
    "    high_corr = []\n",
    "    for i in range(len(corr.columns)):\n",
    "        for j in range(i+1, len(corr.columns)):\n",
    "            val = corr.iloc[i, j]\n",
    "            if abs(val) > 0.8:\n",
    "                high_corr.append((corr.columns[i], corr.columns[j], val))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for f1, f2, val in sorted(high_corr, key=lambda x: -abs(x[2]))[:20]:\n",
    "        print(f'  {f1:20s} - {f2:20s}: {val:.4f}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Feature Policy Compliance Check"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if 'train_df' in locals():\n",
    "    from src.features.build_features import validate_feature_policy\n",
    "    \n",
    "    result = validate_feature_policy(train_df.columns.tolist())\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print('=== Feature Policy Validation ===')\n",
    print(f'Policy Compliant: {result[\"policy_compliant\"]}')\n",
    print()\n",
    "    print(f'Excluded features present: {result[\"excluded_features_present\"]}')\n",
    print()\n",
    "    print(f'FULL_METADATA available: {len(result[\"full_metadata_available\"])}/{len(config[\"feature_sets\"][\"FULL_METADATA\"])}')\n",
    "    if result['full_metadata_missing']:\n",
    "        print(f'  Missing: {result[\"full_metadata_missing\"]}')\n",
    "    print()\n",
    "    print(f'RESTRICTED_METADATA available: {len(result[\"restricted_metadata_available\"])}/{len(config[\"feature_sets\"][\"RESTRICTED_METADATA\"])}')\n",
    "    if result['restricted_metadata_missing']:\n",
    "        print(f'  Missing: {result[\"restricted_metadata_missing\"]}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Initial Observations"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Key Observations:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Class Balance**: Check if the dataset is balanced or imbalanced between normal and anomaly classes.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Feature Availability**: Verify which metadata features are available in the dataset vs. our feature policy.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Missing Values**: Identify any columns with missing data that need handling.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **Feature Distributions**: Observe how metadata features differ between normal and anomalous traffic.\n",
    "\n",
    "5. **Categorical Features**: Understand the distribution of protocol, service, and connection state.\n",
    "\n",
    "6. **Correlations**: Identify highly correlated features that may cause multicollinearity.\n",
    "\n",
    "7. **Policy Compliance**: Ensure no excluded features (IP addresses, payload content) are accidentally included.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "**Next Steps:**\n",
    "- Run the full pipeline: `python -m src.pipeline`\n",
    "- This will execute preprocessing, training, evaluation, and generate plots\n",
    "- All results will be saved to `results/` directory\n",
    "- The README will be updated with actual experimental results"
   ]
  }
